1
00:00:01,001 --> 00:00:03,336
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:03,420 --> 00:00:06,464
[tense music playing]

3
00:00:20,353 --> 00:00:21,521
[screaming]

4
00:00:21,604 --> 00:00:23,773
[shattering sound]

5
00:00:27,777 --> 00:00:32,323
[Diego] <i>The Ardientes were after me.</i>
<i>No one else should've gotten involved.</i>

6
00:00:32,407 --> 00:00:34,242
<i>I'll go face them</i>
<i>so no one else gets hurt.</i>

7
00:00:34,325 --> 00:00:35,660
[Anna] <i>Don't blame yourself.</i>

8
00:00:35,744 --> 00:00:38,705
<i>What the Ardientes did was not your fault!</i>

9
00:00:38,788 --> 00:00:41,374
<i>Don't go, Diego. The people here need you.</i>

10
00:00:41,458 --> 00:00:43,835
<i>I know you can't wait to go</i>
<i>after the Ardientes.</i>

11
00:00:43,918 --> 00:00:45,128
<i>The same goes for me, Jepoy!</i>

12
00:00:45,211 --> 00:00:48,339
<i>But we need to stick to the plan.</i>

13
00:00:48,423 --> 00:00:49,883
<i>Julio won't know what hit him.</i>

14
00:00:50,300 --> 00:00:51,092
[Diego] <i>Divine Uytengco?</i>

15
00:00:51,176 --> 00:00:54,804
[Arthur] <i>Ivy asked me to bring</i>
<i>her here. But she won't talk.</i>

16
00:00:54,888 --> 00:00:57,891
<i>You're better at this.</i>
<i>She might listen to you.</i>

17
00:00:57,974 --> 00:01:01,352
<i>Jaguar was the one who tried</i>
<i>to kill your son.</i>

18
00:01:02,187 --> 00:01:03,313
<i>You betrayed me!</i>

19
00:01:03,396 --> 00:01:04,981
[Raul] <i>That's the gun I gave Madrigal.</i>

20
00:01:05,065 --> 00:01:07,233
<i>He probably did that for personal reasons.</i>

21
00:01:07,317 --> 00:01:09,110
<i>Then kill Madrigal!</i>

22
00:01:09,194 --> 00:01:11,571
[Julio] <i>Colonel Sanggano here</i>
<i>just informed me</i>

23
00:01:11,654 --> 00:01:14,824
<i>that they already know</i>
<i>where to find Madrigal.</i>

24
00:01:14,908 --> 00:01:18,203
<i>Let's go make that bastard suffer.</i>

25
00:01:18,286 --> 00:01:20,955
<i>What's the problem?</i>
<i>If this is the way my own group</i>

26
00:01:21,039 --> 00:01:22,832
<i>and boss are going to treat me,</i>
<i>then I'll just leave.</i>

27
00:01:24,167 --> 00:01:29,839
<i>Give me Madrigal, or else,</i>
<i>I will book you a one-way ticket to hell</i>

28
00:01:29,923 --> 00:01:32,258
<i>with Satan as your bodyguard.</i>

29
00:01:32,342 --> 00:01:34,886
-[Jepoy] <i>I'm leaving this place.</i>
-[Ivy] <i>Where are you going?</i>

30
00:01:34,969 --> 00:01:37,639
<i>Somewhere far away.</i>
<i>So I can protect you all.</i>

31
00:01:37,722 --> 00:01:39,098
<i>I'll return to the shadows.</i>

32
00:01:43,603 --> 00:01:44,646
[Emilia sighs]

33
00:01:45,438 --> 00:01:48,650
It makes me wonder why up to now,

34
00:01:49,359 --> 00:01:52,278
we still haven't caught
the person who shot Arnaldo.

35
00:01:52,987 --> 00:01:57,659
I'm thinking that person
might just be around us, Papa.

36
00:01:57,742 --> 00:02:00,161
Who knows? You were probably
with them yesterday.

37
00:02:00,245 --> 00:02:02,455
[ominous music playing]

38
00:02:02,539 --> 00:02:07,418
Emilia, if you're alluding to Miss Aguas,

39
00:02:08,670 --> 00:02:10,463
she has cleared herself…

40
00:02:11,965 --> 00:02:12,966
for now.

41
00:02:13,800 --> 00:02:15,176
So, stop picking on her.

42
00:02:16,553 --> 00:02:21,599
Papa, aren't you wondering why
she doesn't want you and Jaguar

43
00:02:21,683 --> 00:02:23,393
to face each other?

44
00:02:24,686 --> 00:02:27,313
What if she's in cahoots with Jaguar?

45
00:02:27,730 --> 00:02:29,691
Plus Diego and Madrigal?

46
00:02:29,941 --> 00:02:31,693
[ominous music playing]

47
00:02:32,944 --> 00:02:36,739
You have an overactive imagination.

48
00:02:38,241 --> 00:02:40,577
You know, just to satisfy you
because you're so annoying,

49
00:02:40,910 --> 00:02:42,745
and since you hate her that much,

50
00:02:43,788 --> 00:02:46,332
why don't you keep an eye on Miss Aguas?

51
00:02:46,875 --> 00:02:48,126
So, you'll do something.

52
00:02:48,501 --> 00:02:50,795
What? Me? [laughs] No way.

53
00:02:50,879 --> 00:02:52,755
You've gotta be kidding me,
Papa. I don't want to.

54
00:02:53,047 --> 00:02:54,048
Why?

55
00:02:55,133 --> 00:02:58,386
Are you scared of her?

56
00:02:59,429 --> 00:03:00,263
Me?

57
00:03:00,346 --> 00:03:03,433
Scared of Ivy? Papa, have you forgotten?

58
00:03:03,516 --> 00:03:06,394
I'm a lioness.
She's nothing but a pesky rat!

59
00:03:06,895 --> 00:03:08,688
So why would I be scared of her?

60
00:03:09,606 --> 00:03:12,150
Do you think she's capable
of beating me? Never.

61
00:03:15,653 --> 00:03:16,654
We'll see.

62
00:03:22,827 --> 00:03:24,078
Hey! It's so hot in here!

63
00:03:24,162 --> 00:03:26,581
<i>Let me go! Get me out of this place!</i>

64
00:03:27,457 --> 00:03:28,249
<i>I still have a…</i>

65
00:03:28,333 --> 00:03:31,628
…business to run!
And my children, they need me!

66
00:03:31,711 --> 00:03:33,838
Just let me go! Come on!

67
00:03:37,091 --> 00:03:39,177
[Divine grunting, panting]

68
00:03:39,260 --> 00:03:40,470
These are your kids, right?

69
00:03:41,512 --> 00:03:43,473
Stephanie, Macie, and your youngest?

70
00:03:44,807 --> 00:03:46,476
[tense music playing]

71
00:03:48,269 --> 00:03:49,938
<i>Ever since your husband died…</i>

72
00:03:50,271 --> 00:03:51,773
…they could only depend on you.

73
00:03:53,107 --> 00:03:55,026
And now, what do you think
would happen to them

74
00:03:55,109 --> 00:03:56,361
if you were to die as well?

75
00:03:57,111 --> 00:04:00,573
Where did you get that?!
Leave my children out of this!

76
00:04:00,823 --> 00:04:02,450
<i>I'm not that easy to put down, okay?</i>

77
00:04:02,659 --> 00:04:04,953
Even if you kill me,
which I doubt you can do,

78
00:04:05,453 --> 00:04:07,580
Emilia will take care of my children.

79
00:04:08,331 --> 00:04:10,208
You're quite dumb, Divine.

80
00:04:10,291 --> 00:04:13,086
Do you really think Emilia will help you?

81
00:04:13,670 --> 00:04:14,921
[Diego] <i>What if I tell you…</i>

82
00:04:15,421 --> 00:04:16,923
…that Emilia won't help you?

83
00:04:17,465 --> 00:04:20,802
Impossible. Emilia owes me a lot!

84
00:04:21,803 --> 00:04:22,804
[Divine] <i>Huh?!</i>

85
00:04:25,974 --> 00:04:26,849
Good point.

86
00:04:27,558 --> 00:04:31,771
You only deposited millions
of pesos to your bank account

87
00:04:31,854 --> 00:04:33,940
just to give it to her. Am I right?

88
00:04:34,023 --> 00:04:35,733
[tense music playing]

89
00:04:36,276 --> 00:04:38,945
We have a copy of all
your bank transactions.

90
00:04:39,946 --> 00:04:41,281
Aren't you ashamed?

91
00:04:41,906 --> 00:04:45,576
You stole the people's money.
Don't you feel guilty?

92
00:04:45,660 --> 00:04:47,245
Why would I be?!

93
00:04:49,289 --> 00:04:51,874
This whole town's money
isn't enough to pay

94
00:04:51,958 --> 00:04:54,502
for everything Emilia Ardiente owes me!

95
00:04:55,086 --> 00:04:56,796
[tense music playing]

96
00:05:02,510 --> 00:05:04,137
You won't get anything from me!

97
00:05:05,847 --> 00:05:07,181
So, let me go!

98
00:05:07,557 --> 00:05:10,101
Let me go and leave
my children out of this!

99
00:05:10,601 --> 00:05:13,479
Well, Arthur? What should we do
with these three?

100
00:05:17,608 --> 00:05:19,777
If you hurt my children,
I'll make sure you'll pay!

101
00:05:20,194 --> 00:05:23,114
<i>If you do something to my children,</i>

102
00:05:23,197 --> 00:05:24,866
<i>I'll make sure your whole family pays!</i>

103
00:05:29,662 --> 00:05:30,788
Take a look at this.

104
00:05:31,956 --> 00:05:34,083
Divine Uytengco's husband reportedly died

105
00:05:34,167 --> 00:05:35,710
of a heart attack.

106
00:05:36,502 --> 00:05:40,506
But he was healthy and had
no history of any illnesses.

107
00:05:41,841 --> 00:05:43,342
That's why I was wondering…

108
00:05:43,801 --> 00:05:45,136
what really happened

109
00:05:45,219 --> 00:05:47,013
to Divine Uytengco's husband.

110
00:05:47,972 --> 00:05:49,932
<i>He may have suffered</i>
<i>the same fate as my father.</i>

111
00:05:50,391 --> 00:05:53,311
[Camia] <i>Get out of here!</i>
<i>You killed my husband!</i>

112
00:05:53,394 --> 00:05:55,480
<i>You killed my husband!</i>

113
00:05:56,314 --> 00:05:59,942
I have a strong hunch Emilia
is also responsible…

114
00:06:00,943 --> 00:06:03,071
for the death of Divine's husband.

115
00:06:05,990 --> 00:06:10,036
I don't understand.
Why would she defend Emilia?

116
00:06:11,037 --> 00:06:15,666
If… If I mention this to Mrs.
Uytengco, she might speak up.

117
00:06:16,918 --> 00:06:21,380
No, Diego. I have something else in mind.

118
00:06:23,758 --> 00:06:25,176
In case you haven't noticed,

119
00:06:26,511 --> 00:06:29,847
if you observe Divine carefully,
she's all about money.

120
00:06:31,557 --> 00:06:36,104
She'll drop you for the next
big buck in a heartbeat.

121
00:06:38,356 --> 00:06:42,944
So, I'm going to gain
Divine Uytengco's trust.

122
00:06:43,945 --> 00:06:46,906
Gain her trust? By bribing her?

123
00:06:47,615 --> 00:06:50,660
I'll buy her off or do whatever it takes

124
00:06:51,285 --> 00:06:52,829
to get her on our side.

125
00:06:59,293 --> 00:07:01,963
Make sure it's nice, okay? Okay, good.

126
00:07:02,338 --> 00:07:03,506
Excuse me. Good afternoon.

127
00:07:03,589 --> 00:07:05,383
Oh, hello. Um, how may I help you?

128
00:07:05,883 --> 00:07:08,719
I'm looking for your most expensive piece.

129
00:07:08,803 --> 00:07:09,846
Okay. Right here.

130
00:07:09,929 --> 00:07:11,597
[tense music playing]

131
00:07:16,519 --> 00:07:17,603
These three?

132
00:07:17,687 --> 00:07:20,314
Yes, but the middle one
is the most expensive.

133
00:07:20,398 --> 00:07:22,066
And, I think it's perfect for you.

134
00:07:22,859 --> 00:07:24,527
[upbeat music playing]

135
00:07:27,738 --> 00:07:29,365
It's really shiny.

136
00:07:35,580 --> 00:07:36,664
And now this too.

137
00:07:37,081 --> 00:07:39,167
Divine and I had an agreement.
It's been ages,

138
00:07:39,250 --> 00:07:41,919
and she still hasn't
kept her part of the deal.

139
00:07:42,753 --> 00:07:44,797
Oh! It's as if you don't know her!

140
00:07:45,131 --> 00:07:46,966
Remember Barcelona last year?

141
00:07:47,300 --> 00:07:49,385
Didn't she go out
with the bartender there?

142
00:07:50,261 --> 00:07:52,638
That's why I came here
to see her daughter.

143
00:07:52,847 --> 00:07:55,183
I'm sure Stephanie knows where her mom is.

144
00:07:55,266 --> 00:07:56,309
Stephanie!

145
00:07:56,392 --> 00:07:58,436
-Hi, Mrs. Emilia!
-Hi.

146
00:08:02,857 --> 00:08:03,774
Where's your Mom?

147
00:08:03,858 --> 00:08:05,526
[tense music playing]

148
00:08:11,240 --> 00:08:12,408
Ivy!

149
00:08:13,075 --> 00:08:14,076
Emilia.

150
00:08:15,036 --> 00:08:16,954
Small world.

151
00:08:17,538 --> 00:08:21,501
What do the millennials call it?
I'm "shookt" to see you.

152
00:08:22,710 --> 00:08:27,924
Well, you can't blame me,
seeing you here in my territory.

153
00:08:28,382 --> 00:08:29,467
And mind you, huh?

154
00:08:29,550 --> 00:08:32,011
In my friend's jewelry shop no less.

155
00:08:32,595 --> 00:08:35,848
You know? I'm really starting
to feel like you're stalking me.

156
00:08:37,141 --> 00:08:40,853
Emilia, what do people do
in a jewelry store?

157
00:08:41,521 --> 00:08:43,814
Buy jewelry, right?

158
00:08:44,232 --> 00:08:47,818
Unless you have a different
definition for this store.

159
00:08:48,528 --> 00:08:52,573
I do. Maybe, um… A boxing ring?

160
00:08:53,658 --> 00:08:58,037
War zone? Or hell? Choose one.

161
00:08:58,120 --> 00:09:01,165
I think it's hell.
You'd feel right at home!

162
00:09:01,249 --> 00:09:02,792
[tense music playing]

163
00:09:03,793 --> 00:09:07,088
It was nice front-stabbing
with you, Emilia.

164
00:09:07,630 --> 00:09:10,675
Excuse me. I'll just spend some money.

165
00:09:11,467 --> 00:09:12,468
Miss?

166
00:09:14,971 --> 00:09:19,308
Is this your most expensive piece?

167
00:09:19,892 --> 00:09:20,893
Huh?

168
00:09:20,977 --> 00:09:22,103
Cheap taste.

169
00:09:22,728 --> 00:09:24,397
[tense music playing]

170
00:09:31,320 --> 00:09:32,280
Where is this place?!

171
00:09:32,363 --> 00:09:33,823
I told you to let me go!

172
00:09:34,115 --> 00:09:35,741
[tense music playing]

173
00:09:40,580 --> 00:09:41,581
Oh.

174
00:09:42,790 --> 00:09:45,459
This is the most expensive
jewelry in my shop!

175
00:09:46,752 --> 00:09:48,963
Did you buy it? Why?

176
00:09:49,505 --> 00:09:50,923
Wasn't this given by your husband?

177
00:09:52,717 --> 00:09:53,759
Listen.

178
00:09:54,552 --> 00:09:58,055
I'll give this back to you
if you cooperate with us.

179
00:10:05,396 --> 00:10:06,939
What do you want to know?

180
00:10:10,401 --> 00:10:12,111
I was the one who bought that.

181
00:10:12,194 --> 00:10:13,988
[dramatic music]

182
00:10:14,071 --> 00:10:17,241
And the one who had you brought here.

183
00:10:18,868 --> 00:10:19,994
Ivy Aguas?

184
00:10:20,620 --> 00:10:22,246
Yes. Oh, yes.

185
00:10:22,872 --> 00:10:23,873
That's right.

186
00:10:29,003 --> 00:10:31,922
Your husband died
of a heart attack, right?

187
00:10:33,090 --> 00:10:34,550
He had a heart attack…

188
00:10:35,718 --> 00:10:38,804
but I heard your husband
was quite healthy.

189
00:10:38,888 --> 00:10:41,515
He didn't even have any ailments.

190
00:10:42,683 --> 00:10:47,521
Makes me wonder if he was yet
another victim of the Ardientes.

191
00:10:48,481 --> 00:10:50,524
[somber music playing]

192
00:10:55,613 --> 00:11:00,951
You think, Divine, that your
husband died of natural causes?

193
00:11:01,869 --> 00:11:05,623
Or are you a victim of the Ardientes too?

194
00:11:06,207 --> 00:11:07,458
[Divine sobbing]

195
00:11:07,541 --> 00:11:10,044
I don't know. I don't know.

196
00:11:12,004 --> 00:11:13,547
Truth is, my husband was a businessman.

197
00:11:13,631 --> 00:11:15,758
-And I was an accountant.
-I know.

198
00:11:15,841 --> 00:11:20,679
And Emilia knew I was envious of her life.

199
00:11:20,763 --> 00:11:24,100
And then she told me
I could have her life.

200
00:11:24,183 --> 00:11:26,102
I could live like a queen.

201
00:11:26,185 --> 00:11:28,312
And then she offered me a proposition.

202
00:11:28,396 --> 00:11:29,980
[tense music playing]

203
00:11:30,064 --> 00:11:32,650
[stuttering] She told me to
transfer billions

204
00:11:32,733 --> 00:11:36,070
of pesos of government funds
to my account.

205
00:11:37,154 --> 00:11:38,948
And live like a queen.

206
00:11:40,366 --> 00:11:41,409
[Divine crying]

207
00:11:42,368 --> 00:11:44,995
My husband and I fought over it.

208
00:11:46,038 --> 00:11:49,667
And then he threatened to expose Emilia.

209
00:11:50,418 --> 00:11:54,964
That's it. That's why Emilia
had your husband killed.

210
00:11:55,047 --> 00:11:57,216
Right? That's what happened, right?

211
00:11:57,299 --> 00:12:00,052
Emilia had your husband killed, Divine.

212
00:12:00,136 --> 00:12:03,305
It's all my fault! It's my fault!

213
00:12:04,056 --> 00:12:07,435
I gave in. I helped her steal money.

214
00:12:08,060 --> 00:12:12,106
I turned a blind eye and pretended
that I didn't see a thing!

215
00:12:13,232 --> 00:12:17,361
What kind of a person am I?
I wasn't like that!

216
00:12:17,820 --> 00:12:22,533
What kind of wife was I?
I allowed all this to happen.

217
00:12:23,492 --> 00:12:25,161
But… What could I do?

218
00:12:25,244 --> 00:12:26,871
I was pushed to a corner.

219
00:12:27,830 --> 00:12:29,248
I was left with no choice.

220
00:12:29,331 --> 00:12:31,125
How can I fight Emilia?

221
00:12:31,208 --> 00:12:33,961
You can fight her.
Because she's just Emilia.

222
00:12:34,044 --> 00:12:35,713
And I am Ivy Aguas.

223
00:12:35,796 --> 00:12:38,257
[tense music playing]

224
00:12:38,966 --> 00:12:41,760
If you agree to my plans,
Divine, if you say yes…

225
00:12:42,636 --> 00:12:47,016
we'll work together,
and we'll bring Emilia down.

226
00:12:49,727 --> 00:12:50,936
[Divine crying]

227
00:12:51,937 --> 00:12:55,691
I promise you, Divine. I will help you.

228
00:12:56,775 --> 00:12:58,110
I'll give you everything.

229
00:13:00,613 --> 00:13:02,239
What about my kids?

230
00:13:05,493 --> 00:13:06,952
We'll protect you.

231
00:13:08,746 --> 00:13:11,457
We'll take care of you and your kids.

232
00:13:13,125 --> 00:13:16,587
I'll protect you. Just trust me, Divine.

233
00:13:17,922 --> 00:13:21,509
[tense music playing]

234
00:13:28,224 --> 00:13:30,226
Aunt Claire, I haven't heard
anything from Divine,

235
00:13:30,309 --> 00:13:31,810
and I'm getting worried.

236
00:13:32,102 --> 00:13:34,355
I'm sure she's okay.

237
00:13:35,022 --> 00:13:36,148
Why don't you call her daughters?

238
00:13:36,232 --> 00:13:39,026
I already did, Auntie, and they
don't know where Divine is.

239
00:13:39,527 --> 00:13:42,321
You know, I just wish she just
got into an accident or maybe,

240
00:13:42,404 --> 00:13:44,031
she was found dead on a sidewalk.

241
00:13:44,406 --> 00:13:45,241
Emilia.

242
00:13:45,324 --> 00:13:48,702
Divine knows a lot
of my secrets, Aunt Claire.

243
00:13:49,453 --> 00:13:53,582
And guess what? I just saw
Ivy Aguas at Divine's shop.

244
00:13:54,250 --> 00:13:55,918
I have a feeling, Aunt Claire,

245
00:13:56,669 --> 00:13:59,380
that someone is going to
use her against me,

246
00:13:59,463 --> 00:14:01,549
and that's Ivy Aguas.

247
00:14:07,763 --> 00:14:09,014
[Georgina] Regarding the criminal case

248
00:14:09,098 --> 00:14:10,474
we filed against Arnaldo,

249
00:14:10,558 --> 00:14:12,184
it will get delayed
because he's in a coma.

250
00:14:12,268 --> 00:14:14,520
Well, Attorney, we should
just file a plunder case

251
00:14:14,603 --> 00:14:16,021
against Emilia first.

252
00:14:16,814 --> 00:14:18,899
It would be harder for Julio Ardiente

253
00:14:18,983 --> 00:14:22,736
to run for office if we expose
Emilia's corrupt deeds.

254
00:14:23,153 --> 00:14:26,615
We'll prepare the evidence
and testimony of Mrs. Uytengco.

255
00:14:26,699 --> 00:14:29,285
We are going to file the case
as soon as possible.

256
00:14:29,368 --> 00:14:32,663
And, Divine, you will be under
witness protective custody.

257
00:14:33,706 --> 00:14:34,748
Thank you, Attorney.

258
00:14:35,875 --> 00:14:38,127
[tense music playing]

259
00:14:39,545 --> 00:14:40,504
[sighs]

260
00:14:40,796 --> 00:14:43,340
Divine. I promise you.

261
00:14:43,424 --> 00:14:44,717
We'll help each other.

262
00:14:46,802 --> 00:14:48,304
We'll take care of you.

263
00:14:49,889 --> 00:14:51,348
Thank you. Thank you.

264
00:14:52,766 --> 00:14:55,144
[Divine] Thank you. Thank you. Thank you.

265
00:14:58,188 --> 00:14:59,440
You know, I really don't wanna hear

266
00:14:59,523 --> 00:15:00,733
about your incompetence, okay?

267
00:15:00,816 --> 00:15:03,319
Just call me once you find Divine.

268
00:15:03,402 --> 00:15:05,195
Understand? Okay?

269
00:15:05,279 --> 00:15:06,697
-[maid] Ma'am! Ma'am!
-Oh, come on!

270
00:15:06,780 --> 00:15:10,200
How many times do I have to
tell you not to bother me if--

271
00:15:10,284 --> 00:15:12,036
-Ma'am.
-What's that?

272
00:15:13,996 --> 00:15:15,122
Read the card.

273
00:15:16,248 --> 00:15:18,792
"My big, bad, naughty girl, Emilia.

274
00:15:19,168 --> 00:15:20,961
I miss your kiss and your big lips--"

275
00:15:21,045 --> 00:15:24,298
That's enough. Give me that.
Get out! Leave!

276
00:15:26,884 --> 00:15:28,677
[ominous music playing]

277
00:15:28,761 --> 00:15:30,095
[giggling]

278
00:15:32,181 --> 00:15:33,474
Emilia, what's that?

279
00:15:34,934 --> 00:15:36,602
[ominous music playing]

280
00:15:37,102 --> 00:15:38,103
Who sent that?

281
00:15:38,395 --> 00:15:40,022
Well, you don't have the right to know.

282
00:15:40,481 --> 00:15:41,941
I'm asking you. Who sent that?

283
00:15:42,232 --> 00:15:43,275
It's from Jaguar.

284
00:15:46,570 --> 00:15:47,780
[Raul] <i>It's from Damian?</i>

285
00:15:48,238 --> 00:15:49,365
[phone ringing]

286
00:15:49,949 --> 00:15:52,409
-I'll take these. Stop that!
-Hey! That's mine.

287
00:15:52,493 --> 00:15:54,078
That's mine, Raul. You don't have--

288
00:15:54,161 --> 00:15:55,120
Wait!

289
00:15:55,204 --> 00:15:56,330
[phone ringing]

290
00:15:58,666 --> 00:16:00,125
-Hey!
-Hello!

291
00:16:00,751 --> 00:16:01,835
Did you like it?

292
00:16:02,127 --> 00:16:03,837
You won't quit it, will you?

293
00:16:04,380 --> 00:16:09,259
I was hoping to talk to Emilia, but fine…

294
00:16:10,219 --> 00:16:12,680
<i>Since you said you won't return…</i>

295
00:16:12,763 --> 00:16:17,726
my mask, and it also seems like
you don't want to return my men,

296
00:16:18,352 --> 00:16:19,728
<i>and my weapons…</i>

297
00:16:20,145 --> 00:16:23,148
maybe you could lend me your wife?

298
00:16:23,232 --> 00:16:25,567
[laughs mockingly]

299
00:16:25,651 --> 00:16:27,903
You bastard! Leave my wife out of this!

300
00:16:27,987 --> 00:16:30,656
If I see you, you're going to get it!

301
00:16:31,156 --> 00:16:32,741
I'm just getting started.

302
00:16:33,409 --> 00:16:36,578
<i>If you don't give back my mask…</i>

303
00:16:37,204 --> 00:16:41,417
you'll feel just how sharp
the Jaguar's fangs are.

304
00:16:42,376 --> 00:16:44,294
<i>I'll take back everything from you…</i>

305
00:16:44,795 --> 00:16:46,463
and even more, Raul.

306
00:16:47,131 --> 00:16:50,509
I'll cut your fake fangs with a saw.

307
00:16:50,592 --> 00:16:52,970
You bastard! Face me man-to-man!

308
00:16:53,053 --> 00:16:54,138
Leave my wife out of this!

309
00:16:54,221 --> 00:16:55,431
-[Damian] <i>Just wait for it.</i>
-Give it--

310
00:16:55,514 --> 00:16:58,559
-Hello!
-[singsongs] Just wait for it.

311
00:16:59,184 --> 00:17:00,644
[laughs mockingly]

312
00:17:01,103 --> 00:17:01,937
Hello!

313
00:17:06,066 --> 00:17:09,194
Tomas, keep an eye on Raul's group.

314
00:17:09,278 --> 00:17:11,030
Find out if they're planning something.

315
00:17:12,031 --> 00:17:14,408
And just like what I did to Emilia…

316
00:17:14,867 --> 00:17:16,326
I will also sabotage their plans.

317
00:17:17,578 --> 00:17:18,704
Is that clear?

318
00:17:19,121 --> 00:17:20,164
Yes, boss.

319
00:17:20,247 --> 00:17:21,582
[tense music playing]

320
00:17:21,957 --> 00:17:25,461
Then why are you still
standing there?! Move!

321
00:17:28,881 --> 00:17:30,674
[tense music playing]

322
00:17:34,303 --> 00:17:37,473
Give that to me, Raul. That's enough.

323
00:17:37,556 --> 00:17:39,725
You don't have the right
to touch my things!

324
00:17:39,808 --> 00:17:41,435
You're not thinking straight, Emilia!

325
00:17:41,518 --> 00:17:42,478
Huh!?

326
00:17:42,561 --> 00:17:44,730
If that really was from Jaguar,
he wouldn't have

327
00:17:44,813 --> 00:17:48,233
given you a phone.
He already gave you one, right?

328
00:17:49,651 --> 00:17:53,280
Well, he told me his men are
on red alert, that's why I know.

329
00:17:53,572 --> 00:17:55,240
[tense music playing]

330
00:17:56,992 --> 00:18:02,581
There's an impostor?
I remember now. Jenny! Jenny!

331
00:18:02,664 --> 00:18:04,083
-Ma'am?
-Throw these out.

332
00:18:04,166 --> 00:18:05,959
Hurry! Get them out of the house!

333
00:18:08,128 --> 00:18:10,547
Raul. Thank you for warning me.

334
00:18:12,091 --> 00:18:14,718
But… how did you know?

335
00:18:17,971 --> 00:18:19,264
Be more careful next time.

336
00:18:20,599 --> 00:18:22,267
[tense music playing]

337
00:18:34,613 --> 00:18:36,281
[tense music playing]

338
00:18:38,867 --> 00:18:40,702
[man] This guy is wanted. Be careful.

339
00:18:41,578 --> 00:18:42,955
Take a good look at the photo.

340
00:18:43,038 --> 00:18:45,290
-[man] If you see him…
-[woman] Look. One million.

341
00:18:45,374 --> 00:18:47,876
-[man] Sir…
-I could use a million pesos.

342
00:18:47,960 --> 00:18:49,711
Yes, same.

343
00:18:49,795 --> 00:18:52,506
--Post it, so everyone can see.
-I wish we would see him.

344
00:18:52,589 --> 00:18:54,508
[man] Here. Here. Put it here.

345
00:18:54,591 --> 00:18:55,884
Oh, I don't have a phone with me.

346
00:18:55,968 --> 00:18:58,220
[man] This guy is wanted, ma'am.
If you see him, inform us right away.

347
00:18:58,303 --> 00:18:59,471
There's a one-million-peso reward.

348
00:18:59,555 --> 00:19:01,181
[woman] I think this guy's famous.

349
00:19:01,265 --> 00:19:04,143
It's one million pesos if we find him.

350
00:19:05,185 --> 00:19:07,104
I know. What crime did he commit?

351
00:19:07,187 --> 00:19:08,230
Why's the reward so big?

352
00:19:08,856 --> 00:19:11,150
I think he did something really bad.

353
00:19:11,400 --> 00:19:13,360
Hey! Why are you taking that down?

354
00:19:13,652 --> 00:19:14,862
This isn't real. This guy's dead.

355
00:19:14,945 --> 00:19:16,321
-It looks like him.
-Yeah.

356
00:19:17,698 --> 00:19:18,699
That's him!

357
00:19:21,160 --> 00:19:26,039
Ah, hello. Hello, sir? Ah, yes.
We saw the man in the poster.

358
00:19:26,373 --> 00:19:29,960
He's here in Sitio Otso. Yes. Sir. Hurry.

359
00:19:31,962 --> 00:19:35,257
Damian keeps watching my every move.

360
00:19:35,966 --> 00:19:40,637
If I push through with the mission,
I'm as good as dead.

361
00:19:41,096 --> 00:19:42,931
Are you serious about that?

362
00:19:43,515 --> 00:19:44,516
[laughs]

363
00:19:44,892 --> 00:19:46,268
You're too dramatic.

364
00:19:47,186 --> 00:19:49,479
You know, just push through
with the mission.

365
00:19:50,022 --> 00:19:52,900
That way, Damian won't beat you to it.

366
00:19:52,983 --> 00:19:56,111
Because if he does,
he'll get all the money,

367
00:19:56,195 --> 00:19:59,531
which was meant for you.
And we wouldn't want that.

368
00:20:00,324 --> 00:20:02,910
That's why you need
to push through with it.

369
00:20:04,036 --> 00:20:06,788
But I'll have a hard time
because I don't have enough men.

370
00:20:08,165 --> 00:20:13,629
Well, then force Madrigal
to work for you again.

371
00:20:13,712 --> 00:20:15,380
[tense music playing]

372
00:20:15,464 --> 00:20:17,132
Natalie, he shot my son.

373
00:20:18,008 --> 00:20:20,677
I won't allow him to set foot
in this place again.

374
00:20:20,761 --> 00:20:23,680
[scoffs] You're so dramatic. I love it.

375
00:20:24,556 --> 00:20:25,557
Get over it.

376
00:20:26,016 --> 00:20:28,769
Just kill him after the mission.

377
00:20:30,312 --> 00:20:31,313
Right?

378
00:20:36,818 --> 00:20:38,612
[tense music playing]

379
00:20:39,863 --> 00:20:41,156
-Thank you.
-Okay. Thank you.

380
00:20:46,703 --> 00:20:47,704
Jepoy.

381
00:20:48,956 --> 00:20:49,873
Anna?

382
00:20:49,957 --> 00:20:52,167
What are you doing here?
Are you following me?

383
00:20:52,960 --> 00:20:55,712
Lily and Diego managed to make
the whistleblower confess.

384
00:20:56,129 --> 00:20:57,714
We prepared a little something
at the hospital,

385
00:20:57,798 --> 00:20:59,716
so we can tell Auntie Camia the good news.

386
00:20:59,800 --> 00:21:01,176
Come with me.

387
00:21:02,344 --> 00:21:04,096
I can't. Someone might follow us.

388
00:21:04,471 --> 00:21:06,056
[tense music playing]

389
00:21:09,226 --> 00:21:11,436
[phone ringing]

390
00:21:15,524 --> 00:21:16,650
Boss, I found Madrigal.

391
00:21:17,276 --> 00:21:18,610
You know what to do.

392
00:21:19,111 --> 00:21:21,780
Watch him closely. We're on our way.

393
00:21:22,072 --> 00:21:23,156
Yes, boss.

394
00:21:23,991 --> 00:21:25,659
[sinister music playing]

395
00:21:32,958 --> 00:21:34,334
Send them my regards.

396
00:21:35,127 --> 00:21:37,629
All right, you need to go
before someone sees us.

397
00:21:37,713 --> 00:21:40,424
-Jepoy.
-Anna, don't be stubborn.

398
00:21:41,675 --> 00:21:44,428
If the Ardientes catch me,
I'm going down alone.

399
00:21:44,970 --> 00:21:47,431
I can do this. Trust me.

400
00:21:47,514 --> 00:21:50,767
Get going. Go on. Leave.

401
00:21:50,851 --> 00:21:53,937
[tense music playing]

402
00:22:06,283 --> 00:22:07,409
-[man] Got you!
-Here! Here!

403
00:22:07,492 --> 00:22:08,493
Let go of me!

404
00:22:08,577 --> 00:22:09,953
-Don't resist!
-Come with us!

405
00:22:10,037 --> 00:22:10,954
-Anna!
-Let go of me!

406
00:22:11,038 --> 00:22:17,627
-Anna!
-Stop! Jepoy! Stop it! Jepoy!

407
00:22:19,087 --> 00:22:20,047
Jepoy!

408
00:22:20,547 --> 00:22:22,632
-Stop it! Stop, or I'll shoot!
-[Jepoy] No! No! No!

409
00:22:22,716 --> 00:22:23,633
Just take me.

410
00:22:23,717 --> 00:22:25,218
-Jepoy.
-Don't! Just take me!

411
00:22:25,302 --> 00:22:26,094
Take me instead!

412
00:22:26,178 --> 00:22:30,891
Jepoy. Jepoy! Let go of me!

413
00:22:31,850 --> 00:22:33,060
Tell that bastard to get up.

414
00:22:33,143 --> 00:22:34,978
-Get up! Get up!
-[Anna yelping]

415
00:22:35,228 --> 00:22:36,646
[Anna] Let go of me!

416
00:22:39,858 --> 00:22:41,068
[panting] Anna…

417
00:22:41,151 --> 00:22:42,235
-[Julio] Hey!
-[Anna] Jepoy!

418
00:22:42,486 --> 00:22:44,321
-[Julio grunts]
-[Jepoy groans]

419
00:22:46,198 --> 00:22:49,951
[Julio] You arrogant prick!
It was so easy to find you!

420
00:22:50,410 --> 00:22:53,246
All I needed to do was offer a reward!

421
00:22:53,622 --> 00:22:55,665
-That easy, huh?
-[Julio] Yes!

422
00:22:56,249 --> 00:22:58,585
I didn't want to do this here.

423
00:22:58,919 --> 00:23:01,254
But because I've had it with you,

424
00:23:01,338 --> 00:23:03,090
I will kill you right here.

425
00:23:03,757 --> 00:23:06,259
I will hang you in this exact place.

426
00:23:06,343 --> 00:23:08,011
I will let your body rot,

427
00:23:08,095 --> 00:23:10,097
and then I will feed you to the dogs!

428
00:23:10,931 --> 00:23:13,767
But before I do all that… Get him up!

429
00:23:14,726 --> 00:23:16,228
-Come on. Get up!
-[Julio] Hurry!

430
00:23:17,979 --> 00:23:21,483
[Julio] Before I do all that,
I will kill you now.

431
00:23:21,650 --> 00:23:23,235
I'll kill you, first!

432
00:23:23,902 --> 00:23:25,487
[Jose] Congressman, cover!

433
00:23:26,571 --> 00:23:28,281
[tense music playing]

434
00:23:28,365 --> 00:23:29,533
[gunshots]

435
00:23:29,616 --> 00:23:30,742
[bystanders screaming]

436
00:23:31,118 --> 00:23:32,577
-Jepoy!
-[Jepoy] Run!

437
00:23:32,661 --> 00:23:33,620
[Anna] Jepoy!

438
00:23:33,703 --> 00:23:34,704
[gunshots]

439
00:23:35,330 --> 00:23:36,373
[Jepoy] Run!

440
00:23:38,750 --> 00:23:39,960
[gunshots]

441
00:23:40,043 --> 00:23:41,378
[tires screeching]

442
00:23:44,548 --> 00:23:46,174
-Jepoy, get in!
-[Julio] Jaguar!

443
00:23:46,466 --> 00:23:49,803
[gunfire continues]

444
00:23:57,853 --> 00:23:58,770
[Julio] Jaguar!

445
00:23:58,854 --> 00:24:01,481
[gunfire]

446
00:24:01,565 --> 00:24:05,652
[tense music swelling]

447
00:24:06,278 --> 00:24:08,655
[screams in frustration]

448
00:24:09,573 --> 00:24:10,574
Stupid!

449
00:24:10,949 --> 00:24:15,996
[tense music playing]

450
00:24:19,666 --> 00:24:22,836
I'm glad we finally have
a witness against Emilia.

451
00:24:22,919 --> 00:24:24,379
-Auntie.
-Oh, thank you, Diego.

452
00:24:24,462 --> 00:24:26,423
[Loring] And that's not
the only good news.

453
00:24:26,506 --> 00:24:29,968
The doctor says your health is improving.

454
00:24:30,051 --> 00:24:32,929
So, after a little more rest,
you can be discharged.

455
00:24:34,264 --> 00:24:35,307
[chuckling]

456
00:24:40,020 --> 00:24:42,981
[soft music playing]

457
00:24:47,944 --> 00:24:48,945
Diego.

458
00:24:50,030 --> 00:24:51,448
Where's Lily?

459
00:24:56,286 --> 00:25:00,457
I guess it's good she isn't
visiting. It's too dangerous.

460
00:25:01,583 --> 00:25:03,376
[Loring] Please. Eat up.

461
00:25:03,460 --> 00:25:05,629
-So you can leave sooner.
-I'll eat later.

462
00:25:05,712 --> 00:25:07,380
-Oh, hello.
-Mom.

463
00:25:09,424 --> 00:25:10,425
Dear.

464
00:25:12,302 --> 00:25:13,303
Mr. Pandoy.

465
00:25:13,929 --> 00:25:14,888
Lily.

466
00:25:14,971 --> 00:25:19,392
[soft music continues]

467
00:25:29,778 --> 00:25:30,862
Have you eaten, Mom?

468
00:25:30,946 --> 00:25:33,031
Not yet. Join me.

469
00:25:33,406 --> 00:25:35,158
[Ivy and Camia giggling]

470
00:25:37,535 --> 00:25:38,662
Miss Loring, Mr. Pandoy,

471
00:25:38,745 --> 00:25:40,789
thank you for taking care of my mother.

472
00:25:41,289 --> 00:25:43,833
-Don't mention it.
-There's no need to thank us.

473
00:25:44,834 --> 00:25:46,086
-Ivy.
-Ivy, eat.

474
00:25:46,169 --> 00:25:47,379
-Have some noodles.
-Please, keep eating.

475
00:25:48,171 --> 00:25:49,172
Thank you.

476
00:25:49,965 --> 00:25:50,966
Mom.

477
00:25:52,050 --> 00:25:53,718
[Ivy] Come on. Eat.

478
00:25:54,135 --> 00:25:55,387
-Okay.
-[Diego] Dessert?

479
00:25:56,096 --> 00:25:57,722
[sinister music playing]

480
00:26:00,892 --> 00:26:04,020
Boss, thank you for saving me back there.

481
00:26:05,939 --> 00:26:07,023
I owe you my life.

482
00:26:08,650 --> 00:26:11,361
Well, then. How about you pay us back?

483
00:26:12,988 --> 00:26:14,322
Join our operation.

484
00:26:15,907 --> 00:26:18,952
[tense music playing]

485
00:26:31,631 --> 00:26:33,425
You know, I'm just wondering, Aunt Claire…

486
00:26:33,883 --> 00:26:37,554
How did Raul find out
that Jaguar has an impostor?

487
00:26:37,971 --> 00:26:40,557
Only Jaguar knew that he had an impostor.

488
00:26:40,932 --> 00:26:43,393
How could he know that? And before,

489
00:26:43,476 --> 00:26:46,896
it was just okay for Raul
that Jaguar was pursuing me.

490
00:26:46,980 --> 00:26:49,566
And now, all of a sudden, he's so mad.

491
00:26:49,649 --> 00:26:51,359
I don't understand it anymore.

492
00:26:51,943 --> 00:26:53,236
Come on, Emilia.

493
00:26:53,570 --> 00:26:57,157
Just don't bother with
Jaguar One, Jaguar Two,

494
00:26:57,240 --> 00:26:58,908
and especially not Raul

495
00:26:58,992 --> 00:27:01,745
because it will only complicate
all of your problems.

496
00:27:02,412 --> 00:27:03,955
[sighs] I guess you're right.

497
00:27:06,041 --> 00:27:07,042
Mrs. Emilia.

498
00:27:07,292 --> 00:27:09,753
Wow, finally. Any good news?

499
00:27:10,003 --> 00:27:10,962
Madam.

500
00:27:11,046 --> 00:27:13,381
A CCTV camera recorded
Divine Uytengco being kidnapped.

501
00:27:14,007 --> 00:27:16,551
Two men blew the tires
off the bodyguard's cars

502
00:27:16,634 --> 00:27:18,053
so they couldn't follow.

503
00:27:18,595 --> 00:27:19,637
Let me see that.

504
00:27:20,221 --> 00:27:21,931
[ominous music playing]

505
00:27:23,850 --> 00:27:24,726
Huh?

506
00:27:24,809 --> 00:27:27,228
[ominous music playing]

507
00:27:31,566 --> 00:27:33,526
I'm sure Divine isn't the only one

508
00:27:33,610 --> 00:27:35,945
who wants to testify
against the Ardientes.

509
00:27:36,821 --> 00:27:39,866
There are plenty more out there,
victims of the Ardientes.

510
00:27:40,241 --> 00:27:41,284
They want to testify,

511
00:27:41,368 --> 00:27:43,161
but they're scared of getting killed.

512
00:27:43,244 --> 00:27:46,081
That's why every move we make
has to be in secret.

513
00:27:46,498 --> 00:27:47,457
It'll take the Ardientes by surprise.

514
00:27:47,540 --> 00:27:49,209
They won't have time to sabotage us.

515
00:27:49,626 --> 00:27:51,336
We know the Ardientes.

516
00:27:51,920 --> 00:27:53,922
What's important is we have Divine.

517
00:27:54,005 --> 00:27:55,382
Somebody will testify for us.

518
00:27:59,427 --> 00:28:00,970
Mom, that's because of you.

519
00:28:01,763 --> 00:28:04,641
That's because of
your investigation into Emilia.

520
00:28:04,724 --> 00:28:06,768
This is the result of that.

521
00:28:08,061 --> 00:28:09,229
Thank you, Mom.

522
00:28:11,106 --> 00:28:14,359
[somber music playing]

523
00:28:15,693 --> 00:28:16,694
Mom.

524
00:28:17,987 --> 00:28:21,699
Lily… I can't help but be emotional.

525
00:28:22,867 --> 00:28:26,121
If Raul didn't take me and make me weak…

526
00:28:28,081 --> 00:28:29,958
I would have been with you
again much earlier.

527
00:28:31,209 --> 00:28:33,503
All of this would have been over long ago.

528
00:28:34,337 --> 00:28:36,089
Mom, we're here now.

529
00:28:36,756 --> 00:28:39,175
What's important is we're together again.

530
00:28:40,009 --> 00:28:41,094
It's the two of us.

531
00:28:42,095 --> 00:28:43,388
We're taking down the next

532
00:28:43,471 --> 00:28:45,890
Ardiente on our list.

533
00:28:47,100 --> 00:28:50,395
Diego will fight Julio.

534
00:28:51,479 --> 00:28:54,941
And he will win the election.
We will win, Mom.

535
00:28:58,069 --> 00:28:59,863
Lily, I'm so proud of you.

536
00:29:00,488 --> 00:29:02,615
And I'm sure if your father were here,

537
00:29:02,699 --> 00:29:03,950
he'd be proud of you too.

538
00:29:08,621 --> 00:29:10,248
This is all for Dad, Mom.

539
00:29:13,042 --> 00:29:14,461
It's for our family.

540
00:29:15,962 --> 00:29:17,630
[somber music continues playing]

541
00:29:31,144 --> 00:29:33,104
Boss, aren't we going in yet?

542
00:29:35,190 --> 00:29:37,400
It looks like Jaguar's men aren't coming.

543
00:29:38,568 --> 00:29:41,279
The shipment would be wasted
if we let it go.

544
00:29:43,281 --> 00:29:48,203
There's a saying, "The early bird
catches the worm."

545
00:29:49,245 --> 00:29:53,958
But, more importantly, that bird
is beaten by bad timing.

546
00:29:54,709 --> 00:29:55,710
Count down.

547
00:29:56,085 --> 00:29:57,629
Five! Four! Three! Two! One!

548
00:29:57,962 --> 00:29:59,422
Very good! Let's go!

549
00:29:59,756 --> 00:30:01,925
[action music playing]

550
00:30:05,303 --> 00:30:06,387
[man] This is it, boss.

551
00:30:11,309 --> 00:30:12,977
[action music playing]

552
00:30:27,033 --> 00:30:28,034
[man] Okay, be careful.

553
00:30:30,870 --> 00:30:32,747
-Boss, somebody's coming!
-Hurry up!

554
00:30:37,877 --> 00:30:39,003
[man] Cover us.

555
00:30:44,592 --> 00:30:46,427
Are you ready? Let's go.

556
00:30:50,473 --> 00:30:52,225
One, two…

557
00:30:52,725 --> 00:30:53,476
Let's go!

558
00:30:53,560 --> 00:30:54,519
[gunshots]

559
00:31:00,692 --> 00:31:01,818
[Jepoy] Leave no one alive!

560
00:31:03,194 --> 00:31:04,195
Where's the driver?

561
00:31:06,114 --> 00:31:08,408
Do you want to live? Come with us.

562
00:31:09,117 --> 00:31:10,827
[action music playing]

563
00:31:14,664 --> 00:31:15,957
Get in the cars. Close the truck.

564
00:31:17,000 --> 00:31:20,461
[action music playing]

565
00:31:34,058 --> 00:31:39,647
[singing] <i>La, la, la, la, la,</i>
<i>la, la, la, la, la…</i>

566
00:31:39,731 --> 00:31:43,359
<i>La, la, la, la, la!</i>

567
00:31:50,658 --> 00:31:51,659
Lily!

568
00:31:54,203 --> 00:31:55,371
Anna, what happened to you?

569
00:31:56,748 --> 00:31:57,790
It's Jepoy.

570
00:31:59,208 --> 00:32:00,585
What happened to Jepoy?

571
00:32:00,877 --> 00:32:04,756
[tense music playing]

572
00:32:11,763 --> 00:32:13,348
[action music playing]

573
00:32:29,739 --> 00:32:32,367
[tense music playing]

574
00:32:35,495 --> 00:32:36,788
All right, bring the goods out.

575
00:32:40,083 --> 00:32:43,127
[tense music playing]

576
00:32:44,420 --> 00:32:45,713
[Damian makes taunting noise]

577
00:32:48,591 --> 00:32:49,884
[Damian laughs]

578
00:32:50,301 --> 00:32:51,803
You're dead!

579
00:32:54,847 --> 00:32:56,224
[gunshots]

580
00:32:56,975 --> 00:33:01,270
Hey, fake Jaguar! The original's back!

581
00:33:01,813 --> 00:33:04,732
Can you tell me how you fit

582
00:33:04,816 --> 00:33:06,776
that big head of yours inside my mask?

583
00:33:06,859 --> 00:33:08,653
You'd better give it back!

584
00:33:08,903 --> 00:33:11,948
[Raul] You won't get it back!
I'm the only Jaguar here!

585
00:33:12,407 --> 00:33:13,408
You?

586
00:33:13,825 --> 00:33:16,244
[laughing]

587
00:33:16,327 --> 00:33:17,996
Funny, 'cause when I came back,

588
00:33:18,496 --> 00:33:20,581
your men sided with their true master!

589
00:33:20,999 --> 00:33:24,127
Just admit it! You're a little house cat

590
00:33:24,210 --> 00:33:26,838
pretending to be a ferocious jaguar!

591
00:33:28,715 --> 00:33:31,759
[gunfire]

592
00:33:31,843 --> 00:33:37,056
[action music playing]

593
00:33:41,769 --> 00:33:42,895
[both grunting]

594
00:33:47,025 --> 00:33:48,735
[tense music playing]

595
00:33:54,449 --> 00:33:55,450
[grunting]

596
00:34:07,086 --> 00:34:08,337
[both grunting]

597
00:34:19,307 --> 00:34:20,850
[Damian] I won't let you off that easy!

598
00:34:21,642 --> 00:34:24,979
I'll show you just
what a real Jaguar can do!

599
00:34:27,148 --> 00:34:28,858
[tense music playing]

600
00:34:31,402 --> 00:34:32,862
[both grunting]

601
00:34:38,951 --> 00:34:41,621
[grunting]

602
00:34:45,541 --> 00:34:47,668
[action music continues playing]

603
00:34:51,589 --> 00:34:52,548
[gunshot]

604
00:34:54,008 --> 00:34:55,426
-[screaming]
-[gunshot]

605
00:35:04,227 --> 00:35:06,104
-[Jepoy] Hey!
-[gunshots]

606
00:35:10,566 --> 00:35:12,235
[tense music playing]

607
00:35:20,118 --> 00:35:21,119
[Raul] Madrigal!

608
00:35:23,246 --> 00:35:24,080
Boss!

609
00:35:24,163 --> 00:35:26,290
[tense music playing]

610
00:35:26,374 --> 00:35:27,333
What's wrong, boss?!

611
00:35:27,416 --> 00:35:32,463
If not for you, the operation
would have succeeded!

612
00:35:32,547 --> 00:35:35,299
-You did this on purpose, didn't you?!
-No, boss! Why would I do that?!

613
00:35:35,883 --> 00:35:37,301
Quit acting so innocent.

614
00:35:37,385 --> 00:35:40,221
Boss, forgive me
for whatever it is I've done.

615
00:35:41,347 --> 00:35:43,349
I didn't mean to.
I didn't do anything wrong.

616
00:35:43,432 --> 00:35:45,893
[suspenseful music]

617
00:35:45,977 --> 00:35:46,936
Boss, please.

618
00:35:47,603 --> 00:35:49,063
I'll be honest with you.

619
00:35:49,147 --> 00:35:50,731
Yes, I saved you from Julio

620
00:35:51,399 --> 00:35:53,401
so you could help us with this operation.

621
00:35:54,152 --> 00:35:57,613
But, after that,
I was planning to kill you.

622
00:35:58,322 --> 00:35:59,282
Boss.

623
00:35:59,365 --> 00:36:01,450
Because your fate has been decided.

624
00:36:01,993 --> 00:36:03,703
[tense music playing]

625
00:36:10,960 --> 00:36:12,587
Is this really Jaguar's hideout?

626
00:36:14,088 --> 00:36:15,131
Yes, it's here.

627
00:36:15,756 --> 00:36:18,092
I had them followed
after we met at the restaurant.

628
00:36:18,885 --> 00:36:22,138
[action music playing]

629
00:36:23,931 --> 00:36:25,600
Boss, what did I ever do to you?

630
00:36:26,017 --> 00:36:27,518
I've been on your side since the start!

631
00:36:27,602 --> 00:36:29,061
I'm your most loyal man!

632
00:36:29,437 --> 00:36:33,482
To me? Nothing. But to my son? A lot.

633
00:36:36,652 --> 00:36:37,945
Say your prayers.

634
00:36:38,529 --> 00:36:40,489
[tense music playing]

635
00:36:41,699 --> 00:36:42,783
[explosion]

636
00:36:48,247 --> 00:36:49,957
-[Diego] Ivy. Ivy, let's go.
-Jepoy.

637
00:36:51,626 --> 00:36:53,211
[Raul coughing]

638
00:36:53,419 --> 00:36:54,670
[men coughing]

639
00:37:04,764 --> 00:37:05,890
Madrigal!

640
00:37:06,807 --> 00:37:08,142
[man coughing]

641
00:37:08,226 --> 00:37:11,437
[tense music playing]

642
00:37:18,569 --> 00:37:19,362
[Anna crying]

643
00:37:19,445 --> 00:37:23,074
Jepoy! Jepoy!

644
00:37:23,157 --> 00:37:26,202
I hope he got out of there alive!

645
00:37:26,285 --> 00:37:29,664
Diego, we need to help Jepoy!
We need to find him!

646
00:37:30,331 --> 00:37:31,666
[Anna sobbing]

647
00:37:31,749 --> 00:37:32,959
Anna, calm down.

648
00:37:37,880 --> 00:37:38,965
Diego.

649
00:37:39,048 --> 00:37:41,008
Nothing bad's going to happen to him.

650
00:37:41,092 --> 00:37:42,218
Anna, listen here…

651
00:37:42,635 --> 00:37:44,595
As long as we haven't found Jepoy's body,

652
00:37:44,679 --> 00:37:46,097
there's nothing to worry about, okay?

653
00:37:46,514 --> 00:37:48,849
We know what Jepoy's capable of.
He can handle himself.

654
00:37:49,767 --> 00:37:52,186
Jepoy was already there with me.

655
00:37:52,270 --> 00:37:56,482
But I couldn't do anything to help him!

656
00:37:57,275 --> 00:37:59,527
Diego, this is my fault!

657
00:38:00,695 --> 00:38:02,071
Anna, this isn't your fault.

658
00:38:02,154 --> 00:38:04,532
We will save Jepoy, okay?
We will find him!

659
00:38:06,492 --> 00:38:07,618
Diego…

660
00:38:09,620 --> 00:38:10,705
[Anna sobbing]

661
00:38:16,502 --> 00:38:18,254
[tense music playing]

662
00:38:20,965 --> 00:38:23,801
[sensual music playing]

663
00:38:36,981 --> 00:38:38,691
[tense music playing]

664
00:38:41,736 --> 00:38:42,737
[wincing]

665
00:38:50,411 --> 00:38:51,871
[groaning]

666
00:39:02,340 --> 00:39:04,133
[Jepoy] <i>Boss, what did I ever do to you?</i>

667
00:39:04,216 --> 00:39:06,427
[Raul] <i>To me? Nothing. But to my son?</i>

668
00:39:06,886 --> 00:39:08,012
<i>Say your prayers.</i>

669
00:39:08,095 --> 00:39:09,055
[explosion]

670
00:39:15,436 --> 00:39:16,729
[grunting]

671
00:39:22,943 --> 00:39:26,947
[suspenseful music playing]

672
00:39:28,824 --> 00:39:31,369
[soft music playing]

673
00:39:35,164 --> 00:39:38,209
<i>Fine. I'll do what you want.</i>
<i>I'll keep my distance.</i>

674
00:39:38,417 --> 00:39:40,086
<i>Just make sure you keep your word.</i>

675
00:39:40,419 --> 00:39:41,420
<i>So, are we good?</i>

676
00:39:41,879 --> 00:39:43,089
[explosion]

677
00:39:44,256 --> 00:39:45,841
-[Diego] <i>Ivy. Ivy, let's go.</i>
<i>-Jepoy.</i>

678
00:39:52,056 --> 00:39:55,226
[soft music playing]

679
00:40:25,047 --> 00:40:26,132
Ivy.

680
00:40:29,718 --> 00:40:30,803
Anna's fine now.

681
00:40:33,180 --> 00:40:35,266
[soft music continues playing]

682
00:40:43,149 --> 00:40:44,942
I'm just worried about Jepoy.

683
00:40:46,694 --> 00:40:47,820
I hope he's all right.

684
00:40:47,903 --> 00:40:49,405
I hope he's alive somewhere.

685
00:40:51,157 --> 00:40:52,658
Why did this have to happen now

686
00:40:52,741 --> 00:40:55,494
when our plans were going so well?

687
00:41:00,708 --> 00:41:02,001
Ivy, we won't give up.

688
00:41:04,628 --> 00:41:05,963
We'll keep fighting.

689
00:41:41,165 --> 00:41:41,916
Stay strong.

690
00:41:43,626 --> 00:41:46,086
[tense music playing]

691
00:41:48,422 --> 00:41:49,840
[phone ringing]

692
00:41:52,051 --> 00:41:53,469
[phone ringing]

693
00:41:54,220 --> 00:41:55,346
It's Jepoy.

694
00:41:55,429 --> 00:41:56,889
[phone ringing]

695
00:41:58,766 --> 00:41:59,642
Jepoy?

696
00:42:00,184 --> 00:42:02,478
-Ivy.
-Jepoy, where are you?

697
00:42:05,397 --> 00:42:07,399
<i>Jepoy, where are you?</i>
<i>I want you to come home.</i>

698
00:42:07,483 --> 00:42:09,777
<i>And I don't want you</i>
<i>to ever leave again. Understand?</i>

699
00:42:12,446 --> 00:42:13,572
Jepoy, come home.

700
00:42:15,115 --> 00:42:18,077
Ivy… I don't know where I am.

701
00:42:22,164 --> 00:42:23,040
I'll call you later.

702
00:42:24,708 --> 00:42:25,584
Jepoy.

703
00:42:26,752 --> 00:42:27,628
Jepoy.

704
00:42:29,672 --> 00:42:30,631
What did he say?

705
00:42:30,714 --> 00:42:33,676
It was Jepoy, but I don't know
where he is. He didn't either.

706
00:42:34,051 --> 00:42:35,135
But, at least, he's safe.

707
00:42:36,804 --> 00:42:38,430
I hope he's in good hands.

708
00:42:39,056 --> 00:42:41,058
[tense music playing]

709
00:42:42,434 --> 00:42:43,936
What matters is that he's alive.

710
00:42:47,356 --> 00:42:50,234
[tense music playing]

711
00:42:53,404 --> 00:42:55,030
[tense music intensifies]

712
00:43:05,916 --> 00:43:06,917
[door opening]

713
00:43:12,673 --> 00:43:14,341
[tense music playing]

714
00:43:21,849 --> 00:43:22,891
Surprised?

715
00:43:24,810 --> 00:43:26,770
You? Ma'am.

716
00:43:28,147 --> 00:43:31,900
Um, you can say, "Thank you."

717
00:43:36,405 --> 00:43:37,448
Thank you.

718
00:43:37,531 --> 00:43:40,075
[chuckles] You sound so disappointed.

719
00:43:40,951 --> 00:43:43,078
Aren't you happy to see me?

720
00:43:44,496 --> 00:43:46,582
I thought you liked me.

721
00:43:46,957 --> 00:43:49,168
[tense music playing]

722
00:43:50,669 --> 00:43:52,129
I have to go, ma'am.

723
00:43:54,006 --> 00:43:56,300
Not so fast, big boy.

724
00:43:56,467 --> 00:43:57,718
[grunts]

725
00:43:57,801 --> 00:43:59,720
Jaguar may have saved you.

726
00:43:59,970 --> 00:44:03,599
But he just used you for the operation.

727
00:44:04,308 --> 00:44:06,977
And he almost killed you.

728
00:44:07,645 --> 00:44:10,272
If not for me.

729
00:44:10,981 --> 00:44:14,318
So, will you still go back to Jaguar?

730
00:44:18,906 --> 00:44:19,990
What do you want?

731
00:44:26,872 --> 00:44:27,873
Wait.

732
00:44:29,124 --> 00:44:30,209
Don't you like it?

733
00:44:35,589 --> 00:44:38,967
What do you really want?
Why did you save me from Jaguar?

734
00:44:41,428 --> 00:44:44,431
Ma'am, I'll only return a favor once.

735
00:44:44,515 --> 00:44:47,976
So, tell me. What is it that you want?

736
00:44:48,060 --> 00:44:49,770
[tense music playing]

737
00:44:50,813 --> 00:44:51,939
Fine.

738
00:44:53,273 --> 00:44:54,900
I want you to work for me.

739
00:44:56,735 --> 00:44:58,946
Let's take Jaguar down.

740
00:44:59,947 --> 00:45:02,449
[tense music playing]

741
00:45:13,794 --> 00:45:14,795
[sighs]

742
00:45:20,509 --> 00:45:23,262
[tense music playing]

743
00:45:32,187 --> 00:45:36,108
<i>Sleep well, Arnaldo.</i>
<i>And don't ever wake up.</i>

744
00:45:36,191 --> 00:45:37,484
<i>I'll be right here.</i>

745
00:45:37,568 --> 00:45:41,613
<i>To keep my friends close,</i>
<i>and my enemies closer.</i>

746
00:45:41,697 --> 00:45:43,574
[Emilia] <i>Have me investigated?</i>

747
00:45:43,657 --> 00:45:45,284
<i>I don't know why you're still alive!</i>

748
00:45:45,367 --> 00:45:48,287
<i>I won't let someone like you</i>
<i>put me behind bars!</i>

749
00:45:48,370 --> 00:45:49,413
<i>Do you understand?!</i>

750
00:45:50,122 --> 00:45:53,917
[Ivy] <i>You used your wealth</i>
<i>to intimidate others.</i>

751
00:45:54,001 --> 00:45:56,879
<i>But you can't buy justice, Emilia.</i>

752
00:45:56,962 --> 00:45:59,214
<i>Run as far as your legs can carry you.</i>

753
00:45:59,298 --> 00:46:02,134
<i>Now it's time for you to face</i>
<i>the consequences of your crimes.</i>

754
00:46:02,217 --> 00:46:04,470
<i>You cannot do this to me!</i>

755
00:46:04,553 --> 00:46:07,264
[theme music playing]
